{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>ויעפלו.</b> A term of strength; and so ״הִנֵּה עֻפְּלָה״ (Habakkuk 2) — אינג\"ריש בְּלַעַ\"ז, a term of brazenness; and so ״עֹפֶל בַּת צִיּוֹן״ (Micah 4), ״עֹפֶל וָבַחַן״ (Isaiah 32). And the midrash of Tanchuma explains it as a term of darkness — they went in darkness, without permission."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "the la'az אינג\"ריש is Old French engrés, 'bold, presumptuous'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:58.678163634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}